{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-ledger", "file": "references/task-20746363-review.md", "content": "# Session review: compact-output task with varied demonstrations

This session had a test grid partitioned by separator rows/columns, while the demonstrations varied widely in size, palette, and output dimensions. The solver did not establish a consistent tile-to-output correspondence or exact encoding from any demo. It guessed constant/compact patterns, submitted a repeated 4x2 candidate after it was rejected, and requested several more demonstrations without adequately integrating their evidence. Those actions produced incorrect answers and unnecessary cost.

Reusable lesson: for compact partitioned outputs, explicitly enumerate panels, separators, output shape, marker coordinates/counts, and output values for every demo. Keep dimensions, correspondence, selector, and encoding as independent hypotheses. A changed palette/scale across demos may still admit an abstract shared mapping, but do not infer one from appearance. Replay any proposed rule exactly across every complete demo before submitting. After a wrong submission, discard the entire failed rule; never repeat the same grid. Request a demo only when two explicit live hypotheses predict different, answer-relevant results. Maintain the Continual-ARC contract: exactly one legal JSON action on the final line on every turn.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen/play/users/u047/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/task-20746363-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/demo-output-mapping.md", "content": "# Validate the demo's output mapping before transfer

A visually structured demo output is not evidence by itself for reflection, tiling, or stamping. After the first plausible but incorrect submission, reopen the task class and output representation before changing coordinates. Record input/output dimensions, map input rows, columns, objects, or symbols to output cells/regions, and compare that candidate mapping against every available pair. Treat exact full-demo reproduction as a prerequisite for submitting; a coherent pattern that fails even one demo is still an unvalidated guess. If requesting another demo, identify which competing mappings its predicted output would distinguish.
